--- P2 power-up with SCLK / CS frames running BEFORE RSTN is released ---
ASSERT P2.held PASS | while RSTN is low, frames (even config 0x3FF) change nothing: switches open, park ON, no amplifier reset
ASSERT P2.quiet PASS | DAC drivers stay tri-state in reset
ASSERT P2.release PASS | RSTN released while CS is high: nothing moves until the next frame
ASSERT P2.next PASS | the next complete frame configures the chip normally
ASSERT P2.data PASS | conversions correct after the late reset release
--- P2 standing assertions (SCLK 3.000 MHz) ---
ASSERT S1.order PASS | plate reset switch (rst_sw) opens before the sampling TG / Cref TG (tg_on) at every sample
        rst_sw -> tg_on min 3.22 ns; CS fall -> rst_sw 0.99 .. 1.06 ns; spread over the 8 channels 0.061 ns
ASSERT S2.simult PASS | all 8 channels sample within 1 ns of each other (simultaneous sampling, Decision 34)
ASSERT S3.gdn PASS | dummy-unit driver gate dac_gdn = ~tg_on (within 3 ns)
ASSERT T1.edge PASS | trial t of ADC i is evaluated between SCLK edges t+i and t+i+1 (no wrap into the next cycle)
ASSERT T2.settle PASS | DAC edge -> comparator clock >= the analog settling time TSET of this corner
        DAC edge -> comparator clock: min 40.97 ns (TSET 22.6 ns)
ASSERT T3.stable PASS | no DAC driver edge while a comparator evaluates
ASSERT T4.window PASS | every comparator window ends before the next SCLK rising edge
        window end -> next SCLK edge: min 184.68 ns; window width min 6.16 ns (comparator decision TDEC 1.58 ns)
ASSERT T5.width PASS | comparator window >= decision time of this corner
ASSERT T6.open PASS | sampling TG, Cref TG and plate reset open and dummy grounded at every comparator clock
ASSERT T7.driven PASS | all 12 bottoms driven (none tri-state) at every comparator clock
ASSERT T8.count PASS | exactly 12 comparator pulses per ADC in every complete frame
ASSERT T9.release PASS | DAC drivers released at SCLK edge 13+i
ASSERT T10.resume PASS | tracking resumes at SCLK edge 14+i
ASSERT T11.crowbar FAIL | no crowbar (gp low and gn high on one bit) at the driver gates
        crowbar overlaps (PMOS and NMOS gate of one bit both on): 2001 events, longest 0.096 ns
ASSERT T12.contention PASS | sampling TG never on while a bottom-plate driver is on
ASSERT T13.idleclk PASS | no comparator clock while CS is high
ASSERT R1.bbm PASS | record and IPG switch of a channel never on together
ASSERT R2.conv PASS | no routing-switch edge while any ADC is converting
ASSERT R3.glitch PASS | no pulse shorter than one SCLK period on sw_rec / sw_ipg (one-shot trigger), no zero-width hazard on the RTL nets
ASSERT D1.edge PASS | DOUT changes only while SCLK is low (after the falling edge)
ASSERT D2.oe PASS | DOUT_OE = ~CS, DOUT = 0 while CS is high
